8000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1781, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1781, "cached_input": 52194, "input": 53977, "output": 170}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 57626, "other": 423, "system": 36788, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 51691}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 160925}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "15f953cd-11b6-531d-bc7e-1b330b8b70b2", "at": 1795729977.9276533, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 16556, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c965c9a923c3e55767c89a91b94073be", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "5da9058a-5c44-598c-b441-87c6223e71d1", "at": 1795729977.9366481, "until": 1795729979.305155, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 16560, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c965c9a923c3e55767c89a91b94073be", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_018TVoZbGZdjCWMiUgeVTiCy", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 8d75b9b HEAD --stat | tail -2; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1200", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" 2>&1|tail -1; git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 8d75b9b HEAD --stat | tail -2; git diff HEAD~1 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1200"]], "output": "```console\nf3d0342 Outline rev. 5: k* on excess over floor; realised shape; granularity caveat\n6661908 Outline rev. 4: Brief rev. 5, review #4, venue budget\n8d75b9b Outline: headline k bound as |C|/2 throughout\n Outline.md | 20 +++++++++++---------\n 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-*Rev. 4, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 5) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n+*Rev. 4, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 6) and the pre-registration (`experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n-**C2 — The needed k (headline, Q).** On whole held-out groups, standardised and raw-point error of S6+P5 as k grows approaches the floor (all of the model's observed cells in C given, scored on the same T); the smallest k reaching ε (ε = δ and 2δ) is the number the paper reports, with group-bootstrap CI, with k on the axis and k/N alongside; headline k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋ on the pool (≈ N/3 once |T| ≈ N/3; k/N on the axis), larger k only as a labelled supplement.\n+**C2 — The needed k (headline, Q).** On whole held-out groups, standardised and raw-point error of S6+P5 as k grows approaches the floor (all of the model's observed cells in C given, scored on the same T); the smallest k whose **excess over the model's own all-others floor** (same target cells) is ≤ ε (ε = δ and 2δ; an absolute error ≤ δ is unreachable because δ ≤ 0.25 × floor — pre-registration §F) is the number the paper reports, with group-bootstrap CI, with k on the axis and k/N alongside; headline k ≤ ⌊|C|/2⌋ on the pool (≈ N/3 once |T| ≈ N/3; k/N on the axis), larger k only as a labelled supplement.\n-Evidence: (a) synthetic data from the model — predicted vs measured curve, estimation term vs M; (b) the same curve on the real matrix with risk = floor + design + misfit; (c) k*(ε) predicted from the training spectrum and σ² vs empirical k* (with CI) for ε = δ, 2δ; the rule is \"useful\" only if the empirical k* falls inside or near the predicted band.\n+Evidence: (a) synthetic data from the model — predicted vs measured curve, estimation term vs M; (b) the same curve on the real matrix with risk = floor + design + misfit; (c) k*(ε) predicted from the training spectrum and σ² (predicted excess = √(floor² + design(k)) − floor, on T) vs empirical k* (with CI) for ε = δ, 2δ, both defined on the excess over the floor; the rule is \"useful\" only if the empirical k* falls inside or near the predicted band.\n-- **G1 matrix gate.** Post-filter shape reported first. ≥ ~100 models × ≥ 30 tasks with run sets allowing k ≥ 8. Below that: narrow the claims, do not loosen the filter, **and fall back to alternatives named in advance**: other pre-specified MTEB suite definitions as separate matrices (e.g. English-only vs multilingual, a task-type subset) and the generative matrices of G2, so the study still has a main result rather than only a smaller one. N < 60 ⇒ headline only up to ~N/3 and the scope line says so.\n+- **G1 matrix gate.** Post-filter shape reported first (realised and pre-registered: 238 models × 328 text tasks, 45,775 cells, density 0.586, 83 org groups; gate met; N is large because MTEB tasks are fine-grained — 117 are retrieval — so within-family redundancy may make small k/N easy, and the granularity sweep of C6 (task type / task / language level) is part of the headline's scope, not a side check). ≥ ~100 models × ≥ 30 tasks with run sets allowing k ≥ 8. Below that: narrow the claims, do not loosen the filter, **and fall ba\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "b2667ccc-6958-5e80-b6df-e0205ce36b54", "at": 1795729979.0870411, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 16573, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c965c9a923c3e55767c89a91b94073be", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "8f7e642a-e20e-5e80-b009-72358511c992", "at": 1795729979.090198, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 16574, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c965c9a923c3e55767c89a91b94073be", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "ce551097-d17e-5b32-bfd4-63a46dd4db82", "at": 1795729979.095046, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 16575, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "c965c9a923c3e55767c89a91b94073be", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "44fd55d4-f91c-545c-b64d-44e96074be8e", "at": 1795729979.1405404, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 16576, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "c965c9a923c3e55767c89a91b94073be", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes":